WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.390
Learn to model or recognise percent (as a fraction related to hundredths) using

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:10.181
concrete models, pictorial representations and number line and compare and order a

00:00:10.181 --> 00:00:14.173
mixture of common, decimal and percent fractions (up to hundredths)

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:21.331
Out of 100 equally sized squares, 88 are shaded. What percent is shaded? The answer

00:00:21.331 --> 00:00:25.529
is 88 percent. 88 out of 100 means 88 percent.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:32.080
Out of 100 pupils, 40 prefer reading. What percentage is that? Pause and solve it in

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.151
your exercise book.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:38.492
The answer is 40 percent. 40 out of 100 means 40 percent.
